        'I must, in a little time, go to God. What comforts me in this life is that I now see Him by faith; and I see Him in such a manner as might make me say sometimes, I believe no more, I see. I feel what faith teaches us, and in that assurance and that practice of faith I will live and die with Him.',
        'Continue then always with God: it is the only support and comfort for your affliction. I shall beseech Him to be with you. I present my service.'
